,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"blind_id\":\"C052\",\"coverage\":[{\"point\":1,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"States 'all classes share one portfolio, fewer realized gains mean smaller capital gains distributions, helping every class', so the shared portfolio benefits both classes.\"},{\"point\":2,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Gives the required limit: 'Cash-based trading can still realize gains' and 'Mutual fund redemptions are typically cash, forcing sales that realize gains.' It does not claim a basis step-up, so optional subdetail (a) is not contradicted.\"},{\"point\":3,\"credit\":1,\"reason\":\"Makes the benefit conditional: 'The benefit depends on ETF-class redemption volume and which lots are delivered.' The investor/AP tax caveat is optional.\"}],\"central_error\":null,\"local_error\":null,\"grade\":\"correct\",\"rationale\":\"All three required minimums are covered. It has no central error: it affirms a shared portfolio and says embedded gains 'leave the portfolio unrealized' with no step-up claim. The §852(b)(6) mechanism is accurate. Calling the benefit pro rata and noting Rule 18f-3 allocation are reasonable and not material falsehoods. Omitting the optional subdetails (basis of retained securities, MF flows imposing costs on ETF holders, investor/AP gains) does not reduce the grade.\"}","ttft_ms":4000,"type":"result","duration_ms":7837,"uuid":"43d585bf-2b0d-4fd0-9179-c5373be501d0","ttft_stream_ms":1624,"time_to_request_ms":57,"first_content_frame_ms":1624,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
